## Working with Claude Code

This project uses a Claude Code harness scaffolded from [claude-scaffold](https://github.com/ajinkya-t/claude-scaffold).

Key conventions:
- One chat per task; for parallel work, create a `git worktree` and start a fresh Claude session there
{%- if enable_superpowers %}
- Superpowers skills auto-fire. Tier-pinned slash shims in `.claude/commands/` (`/brainstorm`, `/sp-plan`, `/sp-debug`, `/sp-skill` on Opus; `/sp-tdd`, `/sp-implement`, `/sp-subagent`, `/sp-worktree`, `/sp-review-request`, `/sp-review-receive`, `/sp-finish`, `/sp-verify` on Sonnet w/ 1M ctx).
- After implementation: `/review-with-superpowers` → `/security-review` → `/commit` → `/techdebt`
{%- else %}
- `/plan` before non-trivial work, `/review` before `/commit`, `/techdebt` at end of session
{%- endif %}
- Agent instructions live in `AGENTS.md` (vendor-neutral, read by Codex/Cursor/Aider too). It is intentionally terse — every line is injected with every prompt. Detailed routing/conventions live in on-demand skills under `.claude/skills/`.
- Personal overrides → `CLAUDE.local.md` (gitignored). Library docs → use WebFetch on demand; don't guess current APIs.
- Settings, hooks, subagents, and skills in `.claude/`
{%- if chrome_extension %}
- Frontend work: install the Claude in Chrome extension for live-page verification
{%- endif %}
{%- if enable_bmad %}
- For substantial features: consider BMAD Method for spec-first elicitation (https://github.com/bmad-code-org/BMAD-METHOD)
{%- endif %}
{%- if enable_superpowers %}

